  "detail": null,
  "summary": "I reviewed all 9 patients on \"DOAC dose review - week of 10/19/2026\" under RBC-PHARM-07. I changed the dose for 8 and left 1 as it was. Each change was made by modifying the existing order, and each has a signed progress note giving the values used, the rule result and the cited records. No other medications were touched.\n\n**Apixaban (§2)**\n- **Dorothy Ashworth (pt-0040):** Reduced from 5 mg twice daily to **2.5 mg twice daily**. She meets 2 criteria: age 83, and creatinine 1.70 mg/dL (150 µmol/L from the outside lab, St. Brigid, on 10/15). Her weight is 68 kg. New order mr-t0001.\n- **Raymond Duquette (pt-0041):** Reduced from 5 mg twice daily to **2.5 mg twice daily**. He meets no criteria (age 70, 84 kg, creatinine 0.98), but he takes itraconazole (mr-00359). New order mr-t0007.\n- **Walter Kowalczyk (pt-0001):** Reduced from 5 mg twice daily to **2.5 mg twice daily**. He meets 2 criteria: age 84 and a measured weight of 57.6 kg on 10/14. Creatinine is 1.18. New order mr-t0009.\n- **Gregory Lindahl (pt-0045):** Reduced from 5 mg twice daily to **2.5 mg twice daily**. He meets no criteria, but a St. Brigid infectious disease letter dated 9/18 says he takes darunavir boosted with ritonavir. That drug is not in our orders. New order mr-t0011.\n- **Harold Vance (pt-0002):** Increased from 2.5 mg twice daily to **5 mg twice daily**. He meets only 1 criterion (age 82). On 10/20 his measured weight was 143 lb (64.9 kg) and creatinine was 1.21. He had been reduced in February, when creatinine was 1.71 and weight 57 kg. New order mr-t0015.\n\n**Rivaroxaban (§3, creatinine clearance by Cockcroft-Gault)**\n- **Clarence Bauer (pt-0039):** Reduced from 20 mg to **15 mg once daily**. Clearance is 44 mL/min (age 81, measured 59 kg on 10/14, creatinine 1.1). I did not use the 168 lb weight from 10/21 because he reported it by phone and was not weighed. New order mr-t0003.\n- **Frank Delgado (pt-0003):** Reduced from 20 mg to **15 mg once daily**. Clearance is 44 mL/min (age 76, 90 kg, creatinine 1.81 mg/dL = 160 µmol/L from St. Brigid on 10/19). New order mr-t0005.\n- **Eugene Moravec (pt-0038):** Increased from 15 mg to **20 mg once daily**. Clearance is 56 mL/min (age 79, 96 kg, creatinine 1.45). New order mr-t0013.\n- **Marjorie Pellegrino (pt-0043):** No change. Clearance is 59 mL/min (female, age 75, 71 kg, creatinine 0.92), so her current 20 mg once daily is correct. Because nothing changed, I did not write a note.\n\n**Points for you**\n- Mr. Duquette's itraconazole is a 12-week course started 10/06. The 2.5 mg dose is tied to it and should be looked at again when the course ends.\n- Mr. Lindahl's infectious disease clinic asked to be consulted before medicine changes. I did not contact them about the reduction, so you may want to let them know.\n\nNo patient met the condition for a warning to the prescriber (an interacting drug taken while already on 2.5 mg twice daily).",
